---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { organizationLd, breadcrumbLd } from '../lib/seo.mjs';
import { platforms } from '../lib/catalog.mjs';
const title = 'How we check';
const description = 'How every compatibility entry is researched, labeled, and checked by hand before it appears here.';
const crumbs = [{ name: 'Home', href: '/' }, { name: title }];
---
<Layout title={title} description={description} jsonLdNodes={[organizationLd(), breadcrumbLd(crumbs)]}>
  <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />
  <article class="container prose" style="padding-block:var(--space-12)">
    <h1>{title}</h1>
    <p>Every entry is checked by hand against the manufacturer's own listing and the physical battery
      interface before it is published. We never auto-generate compatibility claims.</p>

    <h2>Platform coverage</h2>
    <p>We only publish a platform once at least one row has been hand-verified. Live now:</p>
    <ul>
      {platforms.map((p) => <li>{p.name}</li>)}
    </ul>
    <p>Not yet covered (no hand-verified row exists): Kobalt 24V (Lowe's), Bauer 20V (Harbor Freight),
      Craftsman V20. We add a platform as soon as we can verify a row for it — <a href="/contact">tell us</a>
      if you'd like one prioritized.</p>

    <h2>Fit types</h2>
    <table class="data-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Label</th><th>What it means</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><span class="badge badge--ok">Made for it</span></td><td>Built for this exact battery by the same brand.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="badge badge--fit">Fits as-is</span></td><td>A gadget from another brand whose foot accepts this battery with no adapter.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="badge badge--warn">Needs adapter</span></td><td>Works only with a separate adapter part; we name the adapter in the notes.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>What we record</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Battery platform and category.</li>
      <li>Whether a battery is included in the box.</li>
      <li>Any adapter required, and a short verification note.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>Spotted something wrong? <a href="/contact">Tell us</a> — corrections are prioritized.</p>
  </article>
</Layout>
